Dear Marc,

Thanks so much, the model runs without any problems now. I had my data array and covariates in the right format, but I had assumed that I should use NAs for the covariates where surveys were missing. I replaced the NAs with 0s. So I understand correctly, does the actual value for the missing surveys not matter? If the observation array has NA, does JAGS skip that site x replicate x species combination, it's just that the covariate datasets cannot have NA's in them?

Thanks again,
Tom

On Wed, Aug 31, 2022 at 6:40 AM Marc Kery <marc...@vogelwarte.ch> wrote:
> Dear Tom,
>
> I would do this:
> fill up your data array for the detection/nondetections with NAs for those surveys that are missing relative to a protocol where all sites have the same number of surveys
> then, you organize the observational covariates in arrays of the exact same dimension, but instead of NAs you fill in any number, e.g., a 0.
> This should work. If you have very large data sets and very large number of zeroes, then this approach is wasteful and something slightly more refined is needed.
>
> Best regards  -- Marc
