Hello All,
Thank your for the quick response.

Yes indeed, the traceplota do use a big range. I have try several sizes of chains and ones it's in this state does not move out.

This is what I know about the problem so far, the observation matrix (that it is individual and time specific). When this matrix is constant (the input is an exact probability) the problema seems to be solved, once you start giving more flexibility to the model (changing the exact value to a distribution such as uniform or beta) the jump start to appear. The narrower the distribution, the less common it is.

I would appreciate any idea or comments, I had try several distributions, lengths of chains, blocking parameters, slice sampling... And the problem seems to persist.

Thank you for your time :)

--
Diego

