Dear Matthijs,

not sure. Diego says he uses the implementation of the Jolly Seber model with data augmentation and refers to Chap 10 of the BPA book. Had to look it up of course myself and there on page 327 I find this:

# Likelihood
for (i in 1:M){
# First occasion
# State process
w[i] ~ dbern(psi) # Draw latent inclusion
z[i,1] ~ dbern(nu[1])
# Observation process
mu1[i] <- z[i,1] * p[i,1] * w[i]
y[i,1] ~ dbern(mu1[i])
.....

So, the model for w is what I referred to below. In the BPA, we put a uniform prior on that psi. My suggestion would now be to try that scale prior instead and see whether that helps.

Best regards  --- Marc

